   "notes": "Busiest airport in Australia with regular wide-body jets (A380, 777, 787, A350, A330). Planes land from the north over the inner west/inner north (Marrickville, Leichhardt, Hunters Hill, Ryde side) and from the south over Botany Bay; the cross runway sends planes over the eastern suburbs and inner west when winds require. Runway end coordinates from SkyVector (0.01 minute precision, about 20 m). New Sydney airspace/flight paths took effect 9 July 2026 to fit in Western Sydney International."
