    "note": "Open for freight since 27 July 2026 (Qantas Freight); first passenger flight is Jetstar to the Gold Coast on 25 October 2026, Air New Zealand from 26 Oct, Singapore Airlines from 23 Nov, Qantas from 28 Mar 2027. It runs 24 hours with no curfew. Flight paths took effect 9 July 2026: by day runway 23 is preferred, so planes land from the north-east over St Marys, Erskine Park, Kemps Creek and the Twin Creeks/Luddenham area and take off towards the south-west. From 11pm to 5:30am 'reciprocal runway operations' are used where safe: planes both land and take off over the south-west (Silverdale, Greendale, Warragamba side) so the heavily populated areas to the north-east get fewer night flights. Luddenham, Twin Creeks, Kemps Creek, Wallacia, Greendale and Silverdale are the closest affected communities; Blue Mountains towns get high-altitude overflights. Noise tools: wsiflightpaths.aerlabs.com and webtrak.emsbk.com/wsi3."
   },
